From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:34:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: restart the second view at a clip join

At a join that is not seamless libbluray reports a discontinuity and the
player resets the demuxer: what the old demuxer had read of both views
is dropped, and the new one reads the base view on from where libbluray
is in the new clip. For 3D the first bytes of that clip are not held
back for it (the hold at a join is for 2D only): the old demuxer
consumed them, and the new one starts a little into the clip. The MVC
extension stream was left where the old demuxer had taken it. Still in
the previous clip, its pictures were paired with the new clip's by
timestamp, which mean nothing across clips: a dependent picture newer
than the base view's held back pairing and every base picture was
dropped until the base view passed it. Already in the new clip (the old
demuxer switched it at its end of file before the reset was handled), up
to 100 dependent pictures read for the new clip went with the old
demuxer, and the base pictures they belonged to were dropped.

The demuxer opened after the reset now tells the input so
(OnDemuxerReset), and the extension restarts in the clip the base view
is in, seeked as at the start of playback, at or before the base view,
so every base picture the new demuxer reads has its second view. An
extension already in that clip is only seeked, not reopened and probed
again. The pictures the old demuxer consumed are not recovered. A seek
and a chapter jump position the extension the same way. In menu mode a
play item, playlist or angle change also opens the demuxer again,
without a discontinuity: the extension restarts there too, where it lost
about 4 s of 3D before.

The extension no longer works through a queue of the play items the base
view entered, which could hold play items of another playlist, or the
clip the restart had just opened, read again from its start at the next
end of file. At its end of file it goes on to the next play item once
the base view has moved past the one it was in, so a short play item is
still played in 3D; after a reset or a seek it opens the clip the base
view is in. The stream setup opens a closed extension, rather than every
play item event of the base view, and the open at the end of opening the
input stays: the demuxer's probe can read the base view past a short
first play item, and the extension must start in that one.

The start time the extension's timestamps are converted with is carried
from one clip's demuxer to the next. It is now set before the demuxer is
opened, so an open that fails does not lose it.

Shared code, unavoidable: the 3D Blu-ray demuxer exists only in
CoreELEC's Kodi (DVDInputStreamBluray, CDemuxMVC, CDemuxStreamSSIF and
their use in DVDDemuxFFmpeg) and has no AML counterpart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
